-- title:
--   Parity character from an even-order generator
-- statement:
--   Let $Q$ be an additive group generated by $b\in Q$. If the additive order of $b$ is even, then
--
--   $$\exists\chi:Q\to\mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z\text{ additive},\qquad\chi(b)=1.$$
--
--   This constructs a parity character from a cyclic presentation.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, https://github.com/alexcour/couret-finite-verifications/blob/65b828d9ffd016ce2a1b05403f303fa5f948c10f/research/correspondants_20261013/lean/CayleyTwoColourParity.lean#L27-L53, lines 27–53; source file SHA-256 d093cc5d0fb31526ef68d4b1d68ee24818c67ebec52adc75170199eecb1ea7a6; theorem Couret.CayleyParity.exists_parity_of_even_generator_order

